# krayt-agent-shellenv (krayt-agent-gemini-cli) — sourced, never executed directly. Shared setup
# between krayt-agent-entrypoint's headless run path and an interactive `krayt shell` session
# (§8.2, add-interactive-shell-session.md decision 14): the entrypoint sources this instead of
# duplicating it, matching the claude-code image (see that image's copy of this file for the full
# reasoning — the two stay in lock-step deliberately, not by accident).
#
# Deliberately NOT `set -e`/`set -u`: this file is SOURCED into the caller's own shell — the
# entrypoint's own subshell for a headless run, or a human's interactive login shell for `krayt
# shell` — so turning those options on here would silently change that shell's behavior out from
# under it. Every step below is written to be safe to fail silently instead, and the entrypoint
# keeps its own `set -euo pipefail` around the `.` that sources this file.
#
# Scoped deliberately narrow (§8.2 "Verify first" #4, add-interactive-shell-session.md): the
# credential materialization from /run/secrets and the KRAYT_CA_CERT / CA-bundle blocks below in
# this image's entrypoint are DEAD CODE under msb ("There is no /run/secrets under msb", §8.2) and
# are NOT ported here — re-exporting what msb's own placeholder-substitution mechanism already set
# in the sandbox's create-time environment would be noise that rots, not a safety net. The one gap
# confirmed without real hardware is `safe.directory` below. Whether an exec'd shell genuinely
# needs anything more — in particular, whether it already inherits the create-time credential env
# var, per "Verify first" #2 — is UNVERIFIED in this environment; see HUMAN_TODO.md. If hardware
# verification finds a real gap, it belongs here, scoped just as narrowly as this one line is.

# The workspace's .git is owned by root (the guest ingests it as root, then makes the tree
# writable), so the non-root agent's/human's own git commands refuse it with "dubious ownership"
# otherwise. Best-effort: a shell with no git installed, or a $HOME that isn't writable yet,
# must still start. KRAYT_WORKSPACE keeps the entrypoint's existing hack/test-entrypoint-
# credentials.sh override working unchanged; an interactive `krayt shell` never sets it and gets
# the real default.
git config --global --add safe.directory "${KRAYT_WORKSPACE:-/workspace}" 2>/dev/null || true
git config --global --add safe.directory '*' 2>/dev/null || true
